# liblevenshtein native API

The C and C++ interfaces provide high-performance approximate string matching
over retained, versioned dictionary resources. This reference was generated
from release **@VERSION@** and covers every public declaration in the installed
headers.

Start with the immutable [C package guide](@SOURCE_URL@/bindings/c/README.md)
or [C++ package guide](@SOURCE_URL@/bindings/cpp/README.md). The
[complete C ABI contract](@SOURCE_URL@/docs/bindings/c-abi-reference.md)
defines every status, precondition, ownership transition, concurrency rule,
complexity bound, batch lease, and callback obligation. The generated pages
below provide declaration-level navigation and source correspondence.

The central lifetime rule is simple: a transducer retains its dictionary
resource, each query cursor retains the immutable revision captured at query
start, and a borrowed batch remains valid only until its exact generation is
released. The C++ wrappers encode those transitions with move-only resource
acquisition is initialization (RAII) objects.
